Hi folks. I have a (hopefully) simple question. Is the goodness-of-fit test using the mb.gof.test() function appropriate for a single-season occupancy model with a removal design? It seems that it might not be; for example, the expected number of detection histories for 1 N/A N/A should actually be inclusive of estimates for other histories (100, 101, 110, 111) impossible with this study design. If this is correct, does anyone have a suggestion for a suitable alternative? Perhaps tweaking the mb.gof.test() function is the best bet.

